.git
**/node_modules
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
frontend/dist
frontend/test-results
frontend/playwright-report
backend/data
backend/.env
**/.env
# backend/ml/models/* (not backend/ml/models, a bare directory match) so the
# !exceptions below actually take effect - Docker does not look inside a
# directory matched by a plain directory pattern. The trained risk model
# (ml/risk_model.py) is the one artifact that ships; everything else that
# could land in this directory (e.g. the rule-distillation surrogate) stays
# out of the image.
backend/ml/models/*
!backend/ml/models/risk_model.joblib
!backend/ml/models/risk_model.json
backend/ml/data
backend/ml/*.csv
*.pdf
